## 4. How to Create Agent Invocations in E2E Tests

### **Pattern 1: Start dispatch engine and post state change**

```typescript
test('should invoke agent on task state change', async ({ request, daemon }) => {
  // Start dispatch engine
  const startResp = await request.post(`${daemon.baseUrl}/api/agent/dispatch`, {
    data: { action: 'start' },
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  });
  expect(startResp.ok).toBe(true);

  // Post a task state change event
  const eventResp = await request.post(`${daemon.baseUrl}/api/agent/events`, {
    data: {
      task_id: '01JXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX',
      task_ref: '@test-task',
      from_status: 'pending',
      to_status: 'in_progress',
      timestamp: Date.now(),
    },
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  });
  expect((await eventResp.json()).accepted).toBe(true);

  // Check status to verify agent was queued/invoked
  const statusResp = await request.get(`${daemon.baseUrl}/api/agent/status`);
  const status = await statusResp.json();
  expect(status.dispatch_enabled).toBe(true);
  // active_invocations or queue_depth > 0 indicates work is happening

  // Clean up
  await request.post(`${daemon.baseUrl}/api/agent/dispatch`, {
    data: { action: 'stop' },
  });
});
```

### **Pattern 2: Bootstrap dispatch (tasks already on disk)**

The dispatch engine's `start()` method automatically evaluates all existing tasks and queues invocations for any matching dispatch rules. No manual event posting needed:

```typescript
// E2E test fixtures in .kspec/ would have tasks with dispatch rules
// When daemon starts, engine bootstraps and queues work automatically
await engine.start();
const status = engine.getStatus();
expect(status.activeInvocations).toBeGreaterThan(0);
```

### **Pattern 3: WebSocket broadcast for real-time updates**

The dispatch engine broadcasts invocation events to WebSocket clients:

```typescript
// Subscribe to 'agents' topic, listen for 'agent_invocation' events
ws.on('message', (msg) => {
  const { type, event_type, data } = JSON.parse(msg);
  if (event_type === 'agent_invocation') {
    // { session_id, agent_id, task_id, status, timestamp }
    // status: "started" | "completed" | "failed"
  }
});
```

